## 17. Transition and License Copies

17.1 No earlier complete public license file was present at the root of the Official Repository when this Version 1.1 draft was prepared. The nested `GUARDIAN-X/pyproject.toml` declared the identifier `LicenseRef-OMEGA-GUARDIAN-X-Proprietary-Alpha` and expected a `GUARDIAN-X/LICENSE` file, while the repository documentation stated that the license file was absent.

17.2 Upon adoption, this License is intended to replace that package metadata identifier for licensable first-party materials in this repository. It does not retroactively authorize earlier conduct or waive accrued claims.

17.3 The root `LICENSE` is the canonical license document for the Official Repository. An identical copy may be placed at `GUARDIAN-X/LICENSE` so that the Python package build can include the license in its wheel. The nested copy is a distribution copy, not a separate or broader grant. If the copies ever differ, the root `LICENSE` controls.

17.4 This License does not change terms for other repositories, independent projects, third-party materials, User Data, Security Materials, or materials the Licensor is not authorized to license. Separate signed agreements, valid prior written permissions, third-party licenses, and Contributor agreements are not silently modified.

